Foundry generates complete, verified Go CLI and TUI repositories from a
declarative Project Specification (foundry.toml).

Command surface:
  init       write a Project Spec TOML to an explicit --out path
  validate   complete pure pipeline; discard plan
  plan       authoritative dry run — Generation Plan, no side effects
  generate   execute the plan (staging, verify, exclusive filesystem place)
  catalog    list or show embedded catalog units
  doctor     check Go pin / FOUNDRY_GO_BIN guidance (advisory)
  version    report version, commit, Go toolchain, catalog digest

plan is the authoritative dry run: inspect the Generation Plan before any
project write. There is no separate dry run command or flag.

The specification path is always explicit via --spec <path|-> (no implicit
working-directory discovery). Stdin is selected with --spec -. init requires
an explicit --out path (also no discovery).

Usage:
  foundry [flags]
  foundry [command]

Available Commands:
  catalog     Inspect the embedded catalog
  doctor      Check Go toolchain pin and FOUNDRY_GO_BIN guidance (advisory)
  generate    Execute the Generation Plan (staging, verify, place destination)
  init        Write a valid Project Spec TOML to an explicit path (flags only)
  plan        Authoritative dry run: print the complete Generation Plan (no side effects)
  validate    Validate a Project Specification through the complete pure pipeline
  version     Print Foundry version, commit, Go toolchain, and catalog digest

Flags:
      --color string    color mode: auto|always|never (text mode only) (default "auto")
  -h, --help            help for foundry
      --output string   output mode: text|json (default "text")
      --quiet           suppress non-essential human output (text mode only)
      --verbose         diagnostic detail on stderr (text mode only)

Use "foundry [command] --help" for more information about a command.
